To fix the **500 Internal Server Error** and the **conflicting server name** warning, you must completely clear your Nginx configuration file. Your `grep` result proves that the domain `aklasbela-tv.com` is written **3 separate times** in that one file, which is causing Nginx to crash.

### 📋 Recovery Plan
1.  **Nginx Cleanse**: We will use a command to empty the file before pasting the clean configuration.
2.  **App Permissions**: Ensure the `www-data` user (Nginx) can actually see your files.
3.  **Backend Verification**: Update the backend to provide a "Debug Page" if it's the one failing.

---

### 🛠️ Execution Steps on your VPS

**1. Wipe the conflicting Nginx file:**
```bash
# This empties the file completely so there are no old duplicates hidden
sudo truncate -s 0 /etc/nginx/sites-available/aklasbela-tv.com
```

**2. Open and Paste the Clean Config:**
```bash
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/aklasbela-tv.com
```
*Paste ONLY this and nothing else:*
```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name aklasbela-tv.com www.aklasbela-tv.com;
    return 301 https://aklasbela-tv.com$request_uri;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name aklasbela-tv.com www.aklasbela-tv.com;

    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/aklasbela-tv.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/aklasbela-tv.com/privkey.pem;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:3005;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }
}
```

**3. Apply and Restart:**
```bash
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl restart nginx
```

---

### 📦 Updated Application Files

